                DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Paragraph(Text("Bakalov-Kac, Twisted Modules over Lattice Vertex Algebras, arXiv math/0402315v1 (2004-02-19): PDF p.8 (4.4), pp.10-13 (4.23),(4.26)-(4.38) give the current, half-field and normalization context. Its pp.4-7 (3.1)-(3.7),(3.13),(3.18)-(3.19), Proposition 3.1 and p.14 Proposition 4.2 concern the still-open fractional products and full twisted reconstruction; those results are not asserted by this unit.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Dong-Nagatomo, Automorphism Groups and Twisted Modules for Lattice Vertex Operator Algebras, arXiv math/9808088v1 (1998-08-19), section 3.2 PDF pp.12-14, especially the displayed oscillator tensor ground and Delta on p.13. Rank/16 is stated in the proof of Theorem 3.13(3), p.19 (the theorem begins on p.18), and is credited there to FLM. This is DN-to-FLM attribution only: neither the FLM nor FHL full text was retrieved.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The finite normal-boundary, current-contraction and induction architecture acknowledges Kalle Kytola, VirasoroProject revision 5ff4245383b2cdd4eea7a0524bc1274c32041eb4, Apache-2.0, through the inspected completed PolynomialFock sources at trureturing revision bfd9ff0f15397a4fb933f36d701a60d325d84b08. The kytola2025virasoro library note identifies this pinned architecture, not an already formalized multicolour half-mode theorem. Formal proof provenance is repo-derived with this acknowledgement.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The existing flm1988monster library note is associated only as a bibliographic and ordinary-lattice background anchor. It is not proof origin for an uninspected FLM or FHL theorem or for the new half-mode matrix proof. The exact BK and DN locators above supply the literature input.")),
            Paragraph(Text("DN p.13 displays a c_mn integrality assertion conflicting with its displayed logarithmic generating function. For F(x,y)=-log((sqrt(1+x)+sqrt(1+y))/2), write its logarithm argument as 1+(x+y)/4-(x*x+y*y)/16 plus terms of total degree at least three. The expansion -log(1+u)=-u+u*u/2 plus higher terms gives F=-(x+y)/4+3*(x*x+y*y)/32+x*y/16 plus higher terms. Thus c10=c01=-1/4 and c11=1/16 are rational. Ordered m,n coefficients and their derivatives must retain both ordered mixed contributions. This is a derived correction, not a published erratum and not an implemented Delta operator.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Charged theta fields, corrected fractional normal products, all-state twisted locality/Jacobi, Y_theta(omega) identification, twisted intertwiners, holomorphic extension, Leech/Monster, anomaly/fusion, full CFT, string theory and the AdS/CFT bridge remain subsequent obligations.")),
            Paragraph(Ref("D5/L/VertexAlgebra/flm1988monster")))));
